From 9a49f61f5d60db0a0c1839a97f20baa0ca6f2f0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RJ Sampson <rj.sampson@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 05:20:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix(cli/keystore): Set BCFIPS-compliant password by default

This changes default behavior of the keystore CLI so that a BCFIPS-compliant
password, "chageitchangeit", is set on keystore creation. On initial create,
we also create the file used by ECK operator to flag that a keystore has
been created so that it does not attempt to overwrite it (if a password
is set on the keystore, ECK operator attempts to create a new keystore on
init).

Signed-off-by: RJ Sampson <rj.sampson@chainguard.dev>
